  "description": "Compact after a memo shrank from many pages to a short value: Mm.M of row 4 receives 20 ASCII characters. Mm: eight rows (ID, Memo M): row 1 Null; rows 2, 6, 7 and 8 with 1000 characters of U+20AC (2000 UTF-16 bytes each); row 3 with 3000; row 4 with 12000; row 5 with the 20 ASCII characters 'twenty chars of text'. Typed lengths and FieldSize are read back. Then DBEngine.CompactDatabase of the mutated file into a work file (the mutated file is unchanged); the public state is read before the mutation, after it and from the compacted file.  Images: 'before' (the fixture copy as given), then one kept image of the closed file after each step; every step opens the database read/write, makes one mutation and closes it, with the DBEngine still alive. The compacted file is kept as a separate derivative (after-compact).",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
